Rename scanbuttond's internal libusb_* symbols to libusbi_*

scanbuttond's USB interface library (libscanbtnd-interface_usb) exports
functions named libusb_init, libusb_open, libusb_close, libusb_exit, ...
On OpenWrt 25.12 the libusb-0.1 API is provided by libusb-compat, which is
implemented on top of libusb-1.0 and calls libusb-1.0's libusb_init/open/
close/exit. Both end up in the same dlopen()ed scope, so libusb-compat's
calls would bind to scanbuttond's functions of the same name.

Purely mechanical rename (s/\blibusb_/libusbi_/) of scanbuttond's own
identifiers in interface/, backends/ and include/; no functional change.
Same idea as jdam6431/scanbuttond (2016), but written against the Debian
0.2.3.cvs20090713-9 tree.
